I approved #9559's plan to cache hashes of the JDK's module files instead of re-hashing about 336 MB on every reuse. Nothing here needs your decision.

A cached hash is trusted only while the file's identity is unchanged: device, inode, size, and modification and change times. I added safeguards borrowed from how git handles the same problem:
- re-hash any file that changed within the file system's timestamp precision of when its hash was cached;
- use the cache only on local disks;
- if the system cannot report a complete identity, always re-hash.

Waiting on: the bisection of the standard-library regression and the end of the #9687 r10 run.
